<title>USA: BASEBALL-HISTORY OF ALL-STAR GAME MOST VALUABLE PLAYERS.</title>
<headline>BASEBALL-HISTORY OF ALL-STAR GAME MOST VALUABLE PLAYERS.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND, Ohio 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>History of All-Star</p>
<p>Game Most Valuable Player Award winners after Sandy Alomar was</p>
<p>named MVP of the 68th Major League Baseball All-Star Game on</p>
<p>Tuesday:</p>
<p>1997 - Sandy Alomar, Cleveland Indians (AL)</p>
<p>1996 - Mike Piazza, Los Angeles Dodgers (NL)</p>
<p>1995 - Jeff Conine, Florida Marlins (NL)</p>
<p>1994 - Fred McGriff, Atlanta Braves (NL)</p>
<p>1993 - Kirby Puckett, Minnesota Twins (AL)</p>
<p>1992 - Ken Griffey Jr., Seattle Mariners (AL)</p>
<p>1991 - Cal Ripken Jr., Baltimore Orioles (AL)</p>
<p>1990 - Julio Franco, Texas Rangers (AL)</p>
<p>1989 - Bo Jackson, Kansas City Royals (AL)</p>
<p>1988 - Terry Steinbach, Oakland Athletics (AL)</p>
<p>1987 - Tim Raines, Montreal Expos (NL)</p>
<p>1986 - Roger Clemens, Boston Red Sox (AL)</p>
<p>1985 - Lamarr Hoyt, San Diego Padres (NL)</p>
<p>1984 - Gary Carter, Montreal Expos (NL)</p>
<p>1983 - Fred Lynn, California Angels (AL)</p>
<p>1982 - Dave Concepcion, Cincinnati Reds (NL)</p>
<p>1981 - Gary Carter, Montreal Expos (NL)</p>
<p>1980 - Ken Griffey Sr., Cincinnati Reds (NL)</p>
<p>1979 - Dave Parker, Pittsburgh Pirates (NL)</p>
<p>1978 - Steve Garvey, Los Angeles Dodgers (NL)</p>
<p>1977 - Don Sutton, Los Angeles Dodgers (NL)</p>
<p>1976 - George Foster, Cincinnati Reds (NL)</p>
<p>1975 - (tie) Bill Madlock, Chicago Cubs (NL), Jon Matlack,</p>
<p>New York Mets (NL)</p>
<p>1974 - Steve Garvey, Los Angeles Dodgers (NL)</p>
<p>1973 - Bobby Bonds, San Francisco Giants (NL)</p>
<p>1972 - Joe Morgan, Cincinnati Reds (NL)</p>
<p>1971 - Frank Robinson, Baltimore Orioles (AL)</p>
<p>1970 - Carl Yastrzemski, Boston Red Sox (AL)</p>
<p>1969 - Willie McCovey, San Francisco Giants (NL)</p>
<p>1968 - Willie Mays, San Francisco Giants (NL)</p>
<p>1967 - Tony Perez, Cincinnati Reds (NL)</p>
<p>1966 - Brooks Robinson, Baltimore Orioles (AL)</p>
<p>1965 - Juan Marichal, San Francisco Giants (NL)</p>
<p>1964 - Johnny Callison, Philadelphia Phillies (NL)</p>
<p>1963 - Willie Mays, San Francisco Giants (NL)</p>
<p>1962 - (2) Leon Wagner, Los Angeles Angels (AL)</p>
<p>1962 - (1) Maury Wills, Los Angeles Dodgers (NL)</p>
<p>(1) - First game</p>
<p>(2) - Second game</p>
</text>
